          "key": "PositioningStrategy::Relative/1",
          "kind": "static",
          "doc": {
            "summary": "Create a strategy for positioning relative to a window.",
            "details": "This method stores a reference to the window and will obtain its bounds dynamically when GetRelativeRectangle() is called, ensuring the position reflects the window's current state.\n\n**Example**\n\n```cpp\nauto window = std::make_shared<Window>();\n// Position menu at bottom of window (no offset)\nauto strategy = PositioningStrategy::Relative(*window, {0, 0});\nmenu->Open(strategy);\n\n// Position menu at bottom of window with 10px vertical offset\nauto strategy2 = PositioningStrategy::Relative(*window, {0, 10});\nmenu->Open(strategy2);\n```",
            "params": [
